  "baseRefName": "master",
  "body": "PR #4 adds a live venture-studio direction while `main` contains the separate service fulfillment/payment runtime. This integration keeps both histories and systems, puts the studio in an npm workspace, and gives the repository one install/check/build entry point.\n\nThe studio repairs address concurrent publishing and partial writes, stale founder/upload authority, private document exposure, generated-code origin escapes, report integrity, and unintended paid execution during setup. Structured reports and browser counters remain evidence inputs rather than independently verified customers or PMF. The current guide is `docs/STUDIO_UPDATE.md`; independent findings and rechecks are in `docs/STUDIO_REVIEW.md`.\n\nValidation: 77 service tests and 77 studio tests pass (154 total), both typechecks/builds and formatting pass, and the eleven-task durable plan passed fresh acceptance checks. Actual Chromium checks verified XML isolation, ES-module loading, private storage add/get/reload and a second browser's isolation. Original deployed migrations 0001\u20130003 are unchanged; repairs add forward migration 0004. Dependency audit reports zero known vulnerabilities.\n\nThe collaborator's existing public dashboard was inspected read-only. These repairs have not been deployed; no paid sessions, outreach or organization changes were performed. Before a production rollout, inspect historical rows against migration 0004 and adapt existing generated products that use direct localStorage/fetch to the scoped product bridge. The integration intentionally preserves existing evidence instead of silently converting old public browser IDs into secret credentials.\n\nLocal startup cleanup adds `npm start`, ignored .env loading with exported-variable priority, and `npm run doctor` without provider calls or credential output. The local studio is running; no Naive key or authorized credit envelope is configured on this machine, so no paid founder was started.\n",
